<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs for Section 3: Ideal Distributions for Fair classification</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We will require a helper result about threshold classifiers to prove our next set of results.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(x,a)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1|X=x,A=a\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(x,a)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1|X=x,A=a\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{ia}=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{ia}=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{ia}(x)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{ia}(x)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the Bayes optimal classifier can be written as <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{*}(x,a)=\mathbb{I}\left(\log\frac{p_{1a}(x)}{p_{0a}(x)}\geq\log\frac{q_{0a}}{q_{1a}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{*}(x,a)=\mathbb{I}\left(\log\frac{p_{1a}(x)}{p_{0a}(x)}\geq\log\frac{q_{0a}}{q_{1a}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(x,a)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1|X=x,A=a\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(x,a)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1|X=x,A=a\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{ia}=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{ia}=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{ia}(x)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{ia}(x)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. We consider group-aware threshold classifiers on <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> of the form <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}(x,a)=\mathbb{I}\left(\eta(x,a)\geq t\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}(x,a)=\mathbb{I}\left(\eta(x,a)\geq t\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be equivalently written as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{t}(x,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{t}(x,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\eta(x,a)\geq t\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\eta(x,a)\geq t\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1\;\big|\;X=x,A=a\right)\geq t\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1\;\big|\;X=x,A=a\right)\geq t\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1\;\big|\;X=x,A=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=0\;\big|\;X=x,A=a\right)}\geq\frac{t}{1-t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1\;\big|\;X=x,A=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=0\;\big|\;X=x,A=a\right)}\geq\frac{t}{1-t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1,X=x,A=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=0,X=x,A=a\right)}\geq\frac{t}{1-t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1,X=x,A=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=0,X=x,A=a\right)}\geq\frac{t}{1-t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=1,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1,A=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=0,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=0,A=a\right)}\geq\frac{t}{1-t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=1,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1,A=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=0,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=0,A=a\right)}\geq\frac{t}{1-t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\frac{p_{1a}(x)}{p_{0a}(x)}\geq\frac{t}{1-t}\cdot\frac{q_{0a}}{q_{1a}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\frac{p_{1a}(x)}{p_{0a}(x)}\geq\frac{t}{1-t}\cdot\frac{q_{0a}}{q_{1a}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\log\frac{p_{1a}(x)}{p_{0a}(x)}\geq\log\frac{t}{1-t}+\log\frac{q_{0a}}{q_{1a}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{I}\left(\log\frac{p_{1a}(x)}{p_{0a}(x)}\geq\log\frac{t}{1-t}+\log\frac{q_{0a}}{q_{1a}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">It is well-known that the group-aware Bayes optimal classifier <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{*}=h_{\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{*}=h_{\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by setting <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, or equivalently,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{*}(x,a)=h_{\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}(x,a)=\mathbb{I}\left(\log\frac{p_{1a}(x)}{p_{0a}(x)}\geq\log\frac{q_{0a}}{q_{1a}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{*}(x,a)=h_{\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}(x,a)=\mathbb{I}\left(\log\frac{p_{1a}(x)}{p_{0a}(x)}\geq\log\frac{q_{0a}}{q_{1a}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now prove Proposition 3.2 from the main paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Proposition 3.2 in the main text) Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y,A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y,A)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the features, class label, and group membership, respectively, of a random data point from any data distribution <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{ia}=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{ia}=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X|Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\Sigma_{ia})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X|Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\Sigma_{ia})</annotation></semantics></math> be multivariate Normal distributions with mean <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{ia}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{ia}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance matrix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{ia}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{ia}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. If the means <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{ia}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{ia}</annotation></semantics></math> and the covariance matrices <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{ia}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{ia}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{ia}^{-1/2}(\mu_{ia}-\mu_{ja})=\Sigma_{ia^{\prime}}^{-1/2}(\mu_{ia^{\prime}}-\mu_{ja^{\prime}})\quad\text{and}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{ia}^{-1/2}(\mu_{ia}-\mu_{ja})=\Sigma_{ia^{\prime}}^{-1/2}(\mu_{ia^{\prime}}-\mu_{ja^{\prime}})\quad\text{and}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{ia}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ja}^{-1}\Sigma_{ia}^{1/2}=\Sigma_{ia^{\prime}}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ja^{\prime}}^{-1}\Sigma_{ia^{\prime}}^{1/2}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{q_{ia}}{q_{ja}}=\frac{q_{ia^{\prime}}}{q_{ja^{\prime}}},~\forall i,j\in\mathcal{Y},a,a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{ia}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ja}^{-1}\Sigma_{ia}^{1/2}=\Sigma_{ia^{\prime}}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ja^{\prime}}^{-1}\Sigma_{ia^{\prime}}^{1/2}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{q_{ia}}{q_{ja}}=\frac{q_{ia^{\prime}}}{q_{ja^{\prime}}},~\forall i,j\in\mathcal{Y},a,a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then the group-aware Bayes optimal classifier on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies equal opportunity.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The Bayes optimal classifier for group <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=a</annotation></semantics></math> in a multi-class setting can be written down as a maximum over posterior probabilities:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{*}(x,a)=\underset{y\in\mathcal{Y}}{\arg\max}~\eta_{y}(x,a),\text{ where }\eta_{y}(x,a)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=y|X=x,A=a\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{*}(x,a)=\underset{y\in\mathcal{Y}}{\arg\max}~\eta_{y}(x,a),\text{ where }\eta_{y}(x,a)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=y|X=x,A=a\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can say that <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{*}(x,a)=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{*}(x,a)=y</annotation></semantics></math>, whenever the following happens:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h^{*}(x,a)=\underset{y\in\mathcal{Y}}{\arg\max}~\eta_{y}(x,a)=\mathbb{I}\left(\frac{\eta_{y}(x,a)}{\eta_{i}(x,a)}\geq 1,\forall i\in\mathcal{Y}\right)=\mathbb{I}\left(\log\frac{p_{ya}(X)}{p_{ia}(X)}\geq\log\frac{q_{ia}}{q_{ya}},\forall i\in\mathcal{Y}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{*}(x,a)=\underset{y\in\mathcal{Y}}{\arg\max}~\eta_{y}(x,a)=\mathbb{I}\left(\frac{\eta_{y}(x,a)}{\eta_{i}(x,a)}\geq 1,\forall i\in\mathcal{Y}\right)=\mathbb{I}\left(\log\frac{p_{ya}(X)}{p_{ia}(X)}\geq\log\frac{q_{ia}}{q_{ya}},\forall i\in\mathcal{Y}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the above simplification, the EO-fairness condition <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pr}\left(h^{*}(X,A)=y\;\big|\;Y=y,A=a\right)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(h^{*}(X,A)=y\;\big|\;Y=1,A=a^{\prime}\right)~\forall y\in\mathcal{Y},a,a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.497em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pr}\left(h^{*}(X,A)=y\;\big|\;Y=y,A=a\right)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(h^{*}(X,A)=y\;\big|\;Y=1,A=a^{\prime}\right)~\forall y\in\mathcal{Y},a,a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> means</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Pr}\left(\log\frac{p_{ya}(X)}{p_{ia}(X)}\geq\log\frac{q_{ia}}{q_{ya}},\forall i\in\mathcal{Y}\;\big|\;Y=y,A=a\right)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(\log\frac{p_{ya^{\prime}}(X)}{p_{ia^{\prime}}(X)}\geq\log\frac{q_{ia^{\prime}}}{q_{ya^{\prime}}},\forall i\in\mathcal{Y}\;\big|\;Y=y,A=a^{\prime}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pr}\left(\log\frac{p_{ya}(X)}{p_{ia}(X)}\geq\log\frac{q_{ia}}{q_{ya}},\forall i\in\mathcal{Y}\;\big|\;Y=y,A=a\right)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(\log\frac{p_{ya^{\prime}}(X)}{p_{ia^{\prime}}(X)}\geq\log\frac{q_{ia^{\prime}}}{q_{ya^{\prime}}},\forall i\in\mathcal{Y}\;\big|\;Y=y,A=a^{\prime}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X|Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\Sigma_{ia})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X|Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\Sigma_{ia})</annotation></semantics></math> are multivariate Normal distributions, their probability densities are</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{ia}(x)=(2\pi)^{-d/2}\det(\Sigma_{ia})^{-1/2}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}(x-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(x-\mu_{ia})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{ia}(x)=(2\pi)^{-d/2}\det(\Sigma_{ia})^{-1/2}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}(x-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(x-\mu_{ia})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we can write</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\frac{p_{ya}(x)}{p_{ia}(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\frac{p_{ya}(x)}{p_{ia}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\left((x-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(x-\mu_{ia})-(x-\mu_{ya})^{T}\Sigma_{ya}^{-1}(x-\mu_{ya})+\log\det(\Sigma_{ia})-\log\det(\Sigma_{ya})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\left((x-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(x-\mu_{ia})-(x-\mu_{ya})^{T}\Sigma_{ya}^{-1}(x-\mu_{ya})+\log\det(\Sigma_{ia})-\log\det(\Sigma_{ya})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\left((\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}r+\mu_{ya}-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}r+\mu_{ya}-\mu_{ia})-r^{T}r-\log\det(\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\left((\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}r+\mu_{ya}-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}r+\mu_{ya}-\mu_{ia})-r^{T}r-\log\det(\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell">        <span id="A1.Ex23.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">by substituting <math id="A1.Ex23.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}r+\mu_{ya}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}r+\mu_{ya}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.Ex23.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d\times d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d\times d})</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}~r^{T}\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}r+(\mu_{ya}-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}r+\frac{1}{2}(\mu_{ya}-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(\mu_{ya}-\mu_{ia})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}~r^{T}\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}r+(\mu_{ya}-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}r+\frac{1}{2}(\mu_{ya}-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(\mu_{ya}-\mu_{ia})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad-\frac{1}{2}r^{T}r-\frac{1}{2}\log\det(\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad-\frac{1}{2}r^{T}r-\frac{1}{2}\log\det(\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let us denote the above expression as <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{yi}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{yi}(r)</annotation></semantics></math>. We can now write the group TPR as:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Pr}\left(\log\frac{p_{ya}(X)}{p_{ia}(X)}\geq\log\frac{q_{ia}}{q_{ya}},\forall i\in\mathcal{Y}\;\big|\;Y=y,A=a\right)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(E_{yi}(R)\geq\log\frac{q_{ia}}{q_{ya}},\forall i\in\mathcal{Y}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Pr}\left(\log\frac{p_{ya}(X)}{p_{ia}(X)}\geq\log\frac{q_{ia}}{q_{ya}},\forall i\in\mathcal{Y}\;\big|\;Y=y,A=a\right)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(E_{yi}(R)\geq\log\frac{q_{ia}}{q_{ya}},\forall i\in\mathcal{Y}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="A1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\sim\mathcal{N}(\bar{0},I_{d\times d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mn>0</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\sim\mathcal{N}(\bar{0},I_{d\times d})</annotation></semantics></math>. Now if we have <math id="A1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dfrac{q_{ya}}{q_{ia}}=\dfrac{q_{ya^{\prime}}}{q_{ia^{\prime}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dfrac{q_{ya}}{q_{ia}}=\dfrac{q_{ya^{\prime}}}{q_{ia^{\prime}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Sigma_{ya}^{-1/2}(\mu_{ya}-\mu_{ia})=\Sigma_{ya^{\prime}}^{-1/2}(\mu_{ya^{\prime}}-\mu_{ia^{\prime}})\quad\text{and}\quad\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}=\Sigma_{ya^{\prime}}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ia^{\prime}}^{-1}\Sigma_{ya^{\prime}}^{1/2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>and</mtext><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{ya}^{-1/2}(\mu_{ya}-\mu_{ia})=\Sigma_{ya^{\prime}}^{-1/2}(\mu_{ya^{\prime}}-\mu_{ia^{\prime}})\quad\text{and}\quad\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\Sigma_{ya}^{1/2}=\Sigma_{ya^{\prime}}^{1/2}\Sigma_{ia^{\prime}}^{-1}\Sigma_{ya^{\prime}}^{1/2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">then the probability of the above event written in terms <math id="A1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\sim\mathcal{N}(\bar{0},I_{d\times d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mn>0</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\sim\mathcal{N}(\bar{0},I_{d\times d})</annotation></semantics></math> becomes identical <math id="A1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall a,a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A},~i\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall a,a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A},~i\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the Bayes optimal classifier satisfies equal opportunity with these set of conditions.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Proposition 3.3 in the main text) Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y,A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y,A)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the features, binary class label, and binary group membership, respectively, of a random data point from any data distribution <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{ia}=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{ia}=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X|Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\sigma_{ia}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X|Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\sigma_{ia}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> be univariate normal distributions, for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the distribution <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">ideal</em> for equal opportunity (see Definition 3.1) if and only if</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mu_{01}-\mu_{11}}{\sigma_{11}}=\frac{\mu_{00}-\mu_{10}}{\sigma_{10}},\quad\frac{\sigma_{11}}{\sigma_{01}}=\frac{\sigma_{10}}{\sigma_{00}},\quad\frac{q_{10}}{q_{00}}=\frac{q_{11}}{q_{01}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>01</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>01</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>00</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>00</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>01</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mu_{01}-\mu_{11}}{\sigma_{11}}=\frac{\mu_{00}-\mu_{10}}{\sigma_{10}},\quad\frac{\sigma_{11}}{\sigma_{01}}=\frac{\sigma_{10}}{\sigma_{00}},\quad\frac{q_{10}}{q_{00}}=\frac{q_{11}}{q_{01}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any cost matrix <math id="A1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathbb{R}^{2\times 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathbb{R}^{2\times 2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the group-aware classifier that minimizes its corresponding cost-sensitive risk is given by <math id="A1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}\left(\eta(x,a)\geq t_{C}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}\left(\eta(x,a)\geq t_{C}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, for a threshold <math id="A1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{C}=(c_{10}-c_{00})/(c_{10}-c_{00}+c_{01}-c_{11})\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>00</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>00</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>01</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{C}=(c_{10}-c_{00})/(c_{10}-c_{00}+c_{01}-c_{11})\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>; see Equation (2) in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>. The distribution <math id="A1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A1.p11.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ideal</em> for equal opportunity if <math id="A1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pr}\left(\eta(X,A)\geq t\;\big|\;Y=i,A=0\right)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(\eta(X,A)\geq t\;\big|\;Y=i,A=1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pr}\left(\eta(X,A)\geq t\;\big|\;Y=i,A=0\right)=\mathrm{Pr}\left(\eta(X,A)\geq t\;\big|\;Y=i,A=1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, for all thresholds <math id="A1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the CDFs are identical, the random variables <math id="A1.p11.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta(X,A)\;\big|\;Y=i,A=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(X,A)\;\big|\;Y=i,A=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p11.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta(X,A)\;\big|\;Y=i,A=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(X,A)\;\big|\;Y=i,A=1</annotation></semantics></math> must be identical. Note that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta(x,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta(x,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1\;\big|\;X=x,A=a\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1\;\big|\;X=x,A=a\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1,X=x,A=a\right)}{\sum_{i=0}^{1}\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,X=x,A=a\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1,X=x,A=a\right)}{\sum_{i=0}^{1}\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,X=x,A=a\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=1,A=a\right)}{\sum_{i=0}^{1}\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=1,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=1,A=a\right)}{\sum_{i=0}^{1}\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{q_{1a}P_{1a}(x)}{\sum_{i=0}^{1}q_{ia}P_{ia}(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{q_{1a}P_{1a}(x)}{\sum_{i=0}^{1}q_{ia}P_{ia}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{q_{1a}\sigma_{1a}^{-1}\exp\left(-\dfrac{(x-\mu_{1a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{1a}^{2}}\right)}{\sum_{i=0}^{1}q_{ia}\sigma_{ia}^{-1}\exp\left(-\dfrac{(x-\mu_{ia})^{2}}{2\sigma_{ia}^{2}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{q_{1a}\sigma_{1a}^{-1}\exp\left(-\dfrac{(x-\mu_{1a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{1a}^{2}}\right)}{\sum_{i=0}^{1}q_{ia}\sigma_{ia}^{-1}\exp\left(-\dfrac{(x-\mu_{ia})^{2}}{2\sigma_{ia}^{2}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1+\exp\left(\dfrac{(x-\mu_{1a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{1a}^{2}}-\dfrac{(x-\mu_{0a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{0a}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{0a}\sigma_{1a}}{q_{1a}\sigma_{0a}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1+\exp\left(\dfrac{(x-\mu_{1a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{1a}^{2}}-\dfrac{(x-\mu_{0a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{0a}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{0a}\sigma_{1a}}{q_{1a}\sigma_{0a}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1+\exp\left(\dfrac{(\mu_{ia}+r\sigma_{ia}-\mu_{1a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{1a}^{2}}-\dfrac{(\mu_{ia}+r\sigma_{ia}-\mu_{0a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{0a}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{0a}\sigma_{1a}}{q_{1a}\sigma_{0a}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1+\exp\left(\dfrac{(\mu_{ia}+r\sigma_{ia}-\mu_{1a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{1a}^{2}}-\dfrac{(\mu_{ia}+r\sigma_{ia}-\mu_{0a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{0a}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{0a}\sigma_{1a}}{q_{1a}\sigma_{0a}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}\dfrac{1}{1+\exp\left(\dfrac{1}{2}\left(\dfrac{\sigma_{0a}^{2}}{\sigma_{1a}^{2}}-1\right)r^{2}-\dfrac{\sigma_{0a}(\mu_{1a}-\mu_{0a})}{\sigma_{1a}^{2}}r+\dfrac{(\mu_{1a}-\mu_{0a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{1a}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{0a}\sigma_{1a}}{q_{1a}\sigma_{0a}}\right)},\quad\text{for $i=0$}\\
\dfrac{1}{1+\exp\left(\dfrac{1}{2}\left(1-\dfrac{\sigma_{1a}^{2}}{\sigma_{0a}^{2}}\right)r^{2}-\dfrac{\sigma_{1a}(\mu_{0a}-\mu_{1a})}{\sigma_{0a}^{2}}r+\dfrac{(\mu_{0a}-\mu_{1a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{0a}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{0a}\sigma_{1a}}{q_{1a}\sigma_{0a}}\right)},\quad\text{for $i=1$}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}\dfrac{1}{1+\exp\left(\dfrac{1}{2}\left(\dfrac{\sigma_{0a}^{2}}{\sigma_{1a}^{2}}-1\right)r^{2}-\dfrac{\sigma_{0a}(\mu_{1a}-\mu_{0a})}{\sigma_{1a}^{2}}r+\dfrac{(\mu_{1a}-\mu_{0a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{1a}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{0a}\sigma_{1a}}{q_{1a}\sigma_{0a}}\right)},\quad\text{for $i=0$}\\
\dfrac{1}{1+\exp\left(\dfrac{1}{2}\left(1-\dfrac{\sigma_{1a}^{2}}{\sigma_{0a}^{2}}\right)r^{2}-\dfrac{\sigma_{1a}(\mu_{0a}-\mu_{1a})}{\sigma_{0a}^{2}}r+\dfrac{(\mu_{0a}-\mu_{1a})^{2}}{2\sigma_{0a}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{0a}\sigma_{1a}}{q_{1a}\sigma_{0a}}\right)},\quad\text{for $i=1$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A1.p11.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X|Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\sigma_{ia}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X|Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\sigma_{ia}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.p11.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\sigma_{ia}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\sigma_{ia}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, for <math id="A1.p11.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta(X,A)\;\big|\;Y=i,A=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(X,A)\;\big|\;Y=i,A=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p11.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta(X,A)\;\big|\;Y=i,A=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(X,A)\;\big|\;Y=i,A=1</annotation></semantics></math> to be identical, we must have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{1}{2}\left(\dfrac{\sigma_{00}^{2}}{\sigma_{10}^{2}}-1\right)R^{2}-\dfrac{\sigma_{00}(\mu_{10}-\mu_{00})}{\sigma_{10}^{2}}R+\dfrac{(\mu_{10}-\mu_{00})^{2}}{2\sigma_{10}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{00}\sigma_{10}}{q_{10}\sigma_{00}}\quad\text{and}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>00</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>00</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>00</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>00</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{1}{2}\left(\dfrac{\sigma_{00}^{2}}{\sigma_{10}^{2}}-1\right)R^{2}-\dfrac{\sigma_{00}(\mu_{10}-\mu_{00})}{\sigma_{10}^{2}}R+\dfrac{(\mu_{10}-\mu_{00})^{2}}{2\sigma_{10}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{00}\sigma_{10}}{q_{10}\sigma_{00}}\quad\text{and}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{1}{2}\left(\dfrac{\sigma_{01}^{2}}{\sigma_{11}^{2}}-1\right)R^{2}-\dfrac{\sigma_{01}(\mu_{11}-\mu_{01})}{\sigma_{11}^{2}}R+\dfrac{(\mu_{11}-\mu_{01})^{2}}{2\sigma_{11}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{01}\sigma_{11}}{q_{11}\sigma_{01}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>01</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>11</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>01</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>01</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>11</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>01</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>11</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>01</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>01</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{1}{2}\left(\dfrac{\sigma_{01}^{2}}{\sigma_{11}^{2}}-1\right)R^{2}-\dfrac{\sigma_{01}(\mu_{11}-\mu_{01})}{\sigma_{11}^{2}}R+\dfrac{(\mu_{11}-\mu_{01})^{2}}{2\sigma_{11}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{01}\sigma_{11}}{q_{11}\sigma_{01}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">as identically distributed for <math id="A1.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, we must also have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{1}{2}\left(1-\dfrac{\sigma_{10}^{2}}{\sigma_{00}^{2}}\right)R^{2}-\dfrac{\sigma_{10}(\mu_{00}-\mu_{10})}{\sigma_{00}^{2}}R+\dfrac{(\mu_{00}-\mu_{10})^{2}}{2\sigma_{00}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{00}\sigma_{10}}{q_{10}\sigma_{00}}\quad\text{and}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>00</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>00</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>00</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>00</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{1}{2}\left(1-\dfrac{\sigma_{10}^{2}}{\sigma_{00}^{2}}\right)R^{2}-\dfrac{\sigma_{10}(\mu_{00}-\mu_{10})}{\sigma_{00}^{2}}R+\dfrac{(\mu_{00}-\mu_{10})^{2}}{2\sigma_{00}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{00}\sigma_{10}}{q_{10}\sigma_{00}}\quad\text{and}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{1}{2}\left(1-\dfrac{\sigma_{11}^{2}}{\sigma_{01}^{2}}\right)R^{2}-\dfrac{\sigma_{11}(\mu_{01}-\mu_{11})}{\sigma_{01}^{2}}R+\dfrac{(\mu_{01}-\mu_{11})^{2}}{2\sigma_{01}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{01}\sigma_{11}}{q_{11}\sigma_{01}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>11</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>01</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>01</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>01</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>01</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>01</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>01</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>01</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{1}{2}\left(1-\dfrac{\sigma_{11}^{2}}{\sigma_{01}^{2}}\right)R^{2}-\dfrac{\sigma_{11}(\mu_{01}-\mu_{11})}{\sigma_{01}^{2}}R+\dfrac{(\mu_{01}-\mu_{11})^{2}}{2\sigma_{01}^{2}}+\log\dfrac{q_{01}\sigma_{11}}{q_{11}\sigma_{01}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">as identically distributed for <math id="A1.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we must have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mu_{01}-\mu_{11}}{\sigma_{11}}=\frac{\mu_{00}-\mu_{10}}{\sigma_{10}}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{\sigma_{11}}{\sigma_{01}}=\frac{\sigma_{10}}{\sigma_{00}}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{q_{10}}{q_{00}}=\frac{q_{11}}{q_{01}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>01</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>00</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>01</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>00</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>00</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>01</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mu_{01}-\mu_{11}}{\sigma_{11}}=\frac{\mu_{00}-\mu_{10}}{\sigma_{10}}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{\sigma_{11}}{\sigma_{01}}=\frac{\sigma_{10}}{\sigma_{00}}\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{q_{10}}{q_{00}}=\frac{q_{11}}{q_{01}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.5.1" class="ltx_text">In the other direction, it is easier to prove that the above conditions imply the distribution to be ideal. It can be proved by simply backtracking the steps above.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs for Section 4</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first derive the KL divergence between two distributions, where each subgroup in the distribution follows a multivariate normal distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y,A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y,A)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the features, binary class label, and binary group membership, respectively, of a random data point from any data distribution <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{ia}=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{ia}=\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X|Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\Sigma_{ia})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X|Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\Sigma_{ia})</annotation></semantics></math> be multivariate Normal distributions with mean <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{ia}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{ia}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance matrix <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{ia}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{ia}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}</annotation></semantics></math> denote a distribution obtained by keeping <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y,A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y,A)</annotation></semantics></math> unchanged and only changing <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X|Y=i,A=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X|Y=i,A=a</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{X}|Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\tilde{\mu}_{ia},\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{X}|Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\tilde{\mu}_{ia},\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\tilde{D}||D\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\tilde{D}||D\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{d}{2}+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{(i,a)}q_{ia}(\tilde{\mu}_{ia}-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(\tilde{\mu}_{ia}-\mu_{ia})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{d}{2}+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{(i,a)}q_{ia}(\tilde{\mu}_{ia}-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(\tilde{\mu}_{ia}-\mu_{ia})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{(i,a)}q_{ia}\left(\mathrm{tr}\left(\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia}\right)-\log\det(\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia})\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{(i,a)}q_{ia}\left(\mathrm{tr}\left(\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia}\right)-\log\det(\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\tilde{D}||D\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\tilde{D}||D\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{(x,i,a)}\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x,\tilde{Y}=i,\tilde{A}=a\right)\log\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x,\tilde{Y}=i,\tilde{A}=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x,Y=i,A=a\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{(x,i,a)}\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x,\tilde{Y}=i,\tilde{A}=a\right)\log\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x,\tilde{Y}=i,\tilde{A}=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x,Y=i,A=a\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{(x,i,a)}\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{Y}=i,\tilde{A}=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x\;\big|\;\tilde{Y}=i,\tilde{A}=a\right)\log\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{Y}=i,\tilde{A}=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x\;\big|\;\tilde{Y}=i,\tilde{A}=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=y,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{(x,i,a)}\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{Y}=i,\tilde{A}=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x\;\big|\;\tilde{Y}=i,\tilde{A}=a\right)\log\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{Y}=i,\tilde{A}=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x\;\big|\;\tilde{Y}=i,\tilde{A}=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=y,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{(x,i,a)}\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)\log\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{(x,i,a)}\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)\log\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(Y=i,A=a\right)\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{(i,a)}q_{ia}\sum_{x}\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)\log\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{(i,a)}q_{ia}\sum_{x}\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)\log\frac{\mathrm{Pr}\left(\tilde{X}=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)}{\mathrm{Pr}\left(X=x\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{(i,a)}q_{ia}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\tilde{P}_{ia}||P_{ia}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{(i,a)}q_{ia}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\tilde{P}_{ia}||P_{ia}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{ia}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{ia}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text"> denotes the distribution of <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\Sigma_{ia})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu_{ia},\Sigma_{ia})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{ia}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{ia}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the distribution of <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{X}\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\tilde{\mu}_{ia},\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{X}\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\sim\mathcal{N}(\tilde{\mu}_{ia},\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia})</annotation></semantics></math>. Their probability densities are</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{ia}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{ia}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(2\pi)^{-d/2}\det(\Sigma_{ia})^{-1/2}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}(x-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(x-\mu_{ia})\right)\quad\text{and}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mtext>and</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(2\pi)^{-d/2}\det(\Sigma_{ia})^{-1/2}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}(x-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(x-\mu_{ia})\right)\quad\text{and}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{p}_{ia}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{p}_{ia}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(2\pi)^{-d/2}\det(\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia})^{-1/2}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}(x-\tilde{\mu}_{ia})^{T}\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia}^{-1}(x-\tilde{\mu}_{ia})\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(2\pi)^{-d/2}\det(\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia})^{-1/2}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}(x-\tilde{\mu}_{ia})^{T}\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia}^{-1}(x-\tilde{\mu}_{ia})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">respectively. Hence, the Kullback-Leibler divergence between <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{ia}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{ia}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{ia}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{ia}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\tilde{P}_{ia}||P_{ia}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\tilde{P}_{ia}||P_{ia}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{E}\left[\log\frac{\tilde{p}_{ia}(\tilde{X})}{p_{ia}(\tilde{X})}\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" lspace="0.280em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{E}\left[\log\frac{\tilde{p}_{ia}(\tilde{X})}{p_{ia}(\tilde{X})}\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}~\mathrm{E}\left[(\tilde{X}-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(\tilde{X}-\mu_{ia})-(\tilde{X}-\tilde{\mu}_{ia})^{T}\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia}^{-1}(\tilde{X}-\tilde{\mu}_{ia})-\log\det(\Sigma_{ia}^{1/2}\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia}^{-1}\Sigma_{ia}^{1/2})\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}~\mathrm{E}\left[(\tilde{X}-\mu_{ia})^{T}\Sigma_{ia}^{-1}(\tilde{X}-\mu_{ia})-(\tilde{X}-\tilde{\mu}_{ia})^{T}\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia}^{-1}(\tilde{X}-\tilde{\mu}_{ia})-\log\det(\Sigma_{ia}^{1/2}\tilde{\Sigma}_{ia}^{-1}\Sigma_{ia}^{1/2})\;\big|\;Y=i,A=a\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
